A||||2||Standard||My amp install pics||||1||
Z||000000||Standard||03-14-2001||11:26 PM||||This is the amp wiring part.  The center console is off, makes things a whole lot easier.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Amp_Wiring.jpg">  <BR>That fuzzy grey blob with the arrow pointing to it is the ground point.  I also used it when I installed my fan switch.  The blue wire is the Amp turn-on wire.  Guess the green text didn't come out too well... d'oh<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Power_cable_routing.jpg">  <BR>There's only one layer of metal to drill through between those wiring harness pass-throughs.  It's a much much easier location to route your power cable through than trying to pass it through one of the shift cable grommetts.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Power_cable_routing_2.jpg">  <BR>Routing in the trunk.  Zip-tie it up so it doesn't come into contact with the exhaust manifold.  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Amp_installed.jpg">  <BR>This is the almost finished product.  When I finally get my sub in there all that speaker wire will be gone, and the rca cable is going to be routed along the passenger side door sill.  With the console on and the passenger seat back, the only place you can see the amp is from the back window, and that's only the heat sink fins and only with some sort of direct light.  <P>Well, feel free to fire any comments/questions my way.  The amp was alot easier to install than I thought it would be.  Fiberglass is a little tricky but the learning curve isn't too steep.  I had to post this in two parts 'cause it wouldn't accept it all in one shot...<P><BR>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-15-2001||08:18 AM||||i don't see a fuse between the battery and the amp.. did you install one? don't want you to smoke yor ride cause of a short! the carpet is easy to poke a hole into, to hide all the wires under...and the center counsel will still fit...<P>what speakers are you running? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||03-15-2001||10:56 AM||||The fuse kinda blends into the battery, it's at the bottom of that loop of wire in front of the battery.  I zip-tied it to another wire for easier access.<P>Right now it's powering my Pioneer 2-way 4x10's.  Even though they're only rated for 35w RMS and I'm giving them 50w RMS they're having no trouble.  For any music that has lots of bass I turn on the 50hz HPF in the deck so I don't blow them, but other than that they sounds damn good.||||reg||1
